# Snort-syntax rules (same file works with real Snort: snort -c ... -R backend/rules/local.rules)
alert tcp any any -> any 80 (msg:"SQL injection attempt"; content:"' or 1=1"; nocase; classtype:web-application-attack; priority:1; sid:1000001; rev:1;)
alert tcp any any -> any 80 (msg:"XSS script tag in request"; content:"<script"; nocase; classtype:web-application-attack; priority:2; sid:1000002; rev:1;)
alert tcp any any -> any 80 (msg:"Directory traversal attempt"; content:"../../"; classtype:web-application-attack; priority:2; sid:1000003; rev:1;)
alert tcp any any -> any any (msg:"Possible TCP SYN port scan"; flags:S; detection_filter:track by_src, count 15, seconds 5; classtype:attempted-recon; priority:2; sid:1000004; rev:1;)
alert tcp any any -> any 22 (msg:"SSH brute force attempt"; flags:S; detection_filter:track by_src, count 6, seconds 30; classtype:attempted-admin; priority:1; sid:1000005; rev:1;)
alert icmp any any -> any any (msg:"ICMP flood"; detection_filter:track by_src, count 20, seconds 2; classtype:attempted-dos; priority:1; sid:1000006; rev:1;)
